  - levelNumber: 14
    chapterNumber: 1
    previousLevel: 13
    accessScore: 80
    inCampaign: 1
    chapterOpen: 1
    id: level_14
    title: LED Protection & Current Limiting
    description: Build a 5 V parallel circuit. Branch A has a replaceable resistor
      in series with a correctly oriented red LED; branch B has a fixed 470 ohm resistor.
      Replace the incorrect 150 ohm resistor with 330 ohm to limit LED-branch current
      to about 9.09 mA (assuming LED forward voltage 2.0 V). Verify about 3.0 V across
      the resistor and 19.73 mA total source current. Switch power off before replacing
      components.
    conditions: Complete all configured objectives. A closed return path is required.
      Source shorts block completion. Target shorts block completion.
    sourceGuid: da2d255690cf0ac4c94790d498db8033
    sourcePath: Assets/My_Assets/_Project_Spark/Prefabs/Levels/Chapter_02/Level_14_Layout/Level_14.asset
    chapter: Electrical Foundations
    accessRule: Open
    layoutPath: Assets/My_Assets/_Project_Spark/Prefabs/Levels/Chapter_02/Level_14_Layout/Level_14_Layout.prefab
    objectives:
    - LED Conducting. LED1 must be forward biased and conducting; visual illumination
      must also be checked in the scene. Connection pair LED_Anode and LED_Cathode.
      Conduction required.
    - "Protected LED Branch Current. Install 330 ohm R_LIMIT so LED branch current
      is 8.0-10.5 mA. current \u2265 8 mA. current \u2264 10.5 mA. Connection pair
      R_LIMIT_Input and R_LIMIT_Output. Conduction required."
    - "Correct Resistor Voltage. Measure 2.7-3.3 V across current-limiting resistor
      R_LIMIT. voltage \u2265 2.7 V. voltage \u2264 3.3 V. Connection pair R_LIMIT_Input
      and R_LIMIT_Output. Conduction required."
    - "Safe Total Consumption. Total supply current must be 18.0-21.0 mA for the
      LED and 470 ohm branches. current \u2265 18 mA. current \u2264 21 mA. Connection
      pair Battery_positive and Battery_negative."
    equipment: []
    concepts:
    - Closed path
    - Ohm law
    - Polarity
    - Measurement
    teachingResources: []
    targets:
    - id: led14_led_conducting
      title: LED Conducting
      description: LED1 must be forward biased and conducting; visual illumination
        must also be checked in the scene.
      kind: ComponentConducting
      componentId: led
      terminalId: 
      positiveId: LED_Anode
      negativeId: LED_Cathode
    - id: led14_limit_current
      title: Protected LED Branch Current
      description: Install 330 ohm R_LIMIT so LED branch current is 8.0-10.5 mA.
      kind: CurrentRange
      componentId: R_LIMIT_Component
      terminalId: 
      positiveId: R_LIMIT_Input
      negativeId: R_LIMIT_Output
    - id: led14_limit_voltage
      title: Correct Resistor Voltage
      description: Measure 2.7-3.3 V across current-limiting resistor R_LIMIT.
      kind: VoltageRange
      componentId: R_LIMIT_Component
      terminalId: 
      positiveId: R_LIMIT_Input
      negativeId: R_LIMIT_Output
