      title: Safe Total Consumption
      description: Total supply current must be 18.0-21.0 mA for the LED and 470
        ohm branches.
      kind: CurrentRange
      componentId: PowerSupply_01
      terminalId: 
      positiveId: Battery_positive
      negativeId: Battery_negative
  - levelNumber: 15
    chapterNumber: 1
    previousLevel: 14
    accessScore: 80
    inCampaign: 1
    chapterOpen: 1
    id: level_15
    title: Dual LED Parallel Circuit Challenge
    description: 'Build two independent LED branches in parallel from a switched
      5 V supply. Branch A uses a replaceable resistor: replace the incorrect 150
      ohm with 330 ohm in Register_Slot_2, then connect the red LED in series. Branch
      B uses a fixed 470 ohm resistor in series with a green LED; correct its polarity.
      Both LED cathodes return to supply negative. Verify both LEDs conduct, each
      branch current is within its target range, and total source current is correct.
      Switch power off before changing parts. Green LED targets depend on its configured
      forward-voltage model.'
    conditions: Complete all configured objectives. A closed return path is required.
      Source shorts block completion. Target shorts block completion.
    sourceGuid: 6284c7018244ffb4a842917d2c9049f8
    sourcePath: Assets/My_Assets/_Project_Spark/Prefabs/Levels/Chapter_02/Level_15_Layout/Level_15.asset
    chapter: Electrical Foundations
    accessRule: Open
    layoutPath: Assets/My_Assets/_Project_Spark/Prefabs/Levels/Chapter_02/Level_15_Layout/Level_15_Layout.prefab
    objectives:
    - Red LED Conducting. Red LED must be correctly oriented and conducting. Fixed
      ID led is reused from the uploaded Level 14 definition; verify the actual Level
      15 scene binding. Connection pair LED_Anode and LED_Cathode. Conduction required.
    - Green LED Conducting. Green LED must be forward biased and conducting. Assign
      fixed ID LED2 to its SparkLED component. Connection pair led_2_Anode and led_2_Cathode.
      Conduction required.
    - "Red Branch Current Safe. Replace the 150 ohm workstation resistor with 330
      ohm. Target 8.0 to 10.5 mA in the red LED branch. current \u2265 8 mA. current
      \u2264 10.5 mA. Connection pair R1_Input and R1_Output. Conduction required."
    - "Green Branch Current Safe. 470 ohm fixed resistor must conduct approximately
      5.5 to 7.0 mA with green LED forward-biased. Calibrate after measuring actual
      SparkLED model. current \u2265 5.5 mA. current \u2264 7 mA. Connection pair
      Resistor_470_Input and Resistor_470_Output. Conduction required."
    - "Correct Total Source Current. Total 5 V source current should be 14.0 to 17.0
      mA once both branches conduct. Calibrate if the green LED forward voltage differs.
      current \u2265 14 mA. current \u2264 17 mA. Connection pair Battery_positive
      and Battery_negative."
    equipment: []
    concepts:
    - Closed path
    - Ohm law
    - Polarity
    teachingResources: []
    targets:
    - id: level15_red_led_conducting
      title: Red LED Conducting
      description: Red LED must be correctly oriented and conducting. Fixed ID led
        is reused from the uploaded Level 14 definition; verify the actual Level
        15 scene binding.
      kind: ComponentConducting
      componentId: led
      terminalId: 
      positiveId: LED_Anode
      negativeId: LED_Cathode
    - id: level15_green_led_conducting
      title: Green LED Conducting
      description: Green LED must be forward biased and conducting. Assign fixed
        ID LED2 to its SparkLED component.
      kind: ComponentConducting
      componentId: led_2
      terminalId: 
      positiveId: led_2_Anode
      negativeId: led_2_Cathode
    - id: level15_red_branch_current
      title: Red Branch Current Safe
      description: Replace the 150 ohm workstation resistor with 330 ohm. Target
        8.0 to 10.5 mA in the red LED branch.
      kind: CurrentRange
      componentId: R1_Component
      terminalId: 
      positiveId: R1_Input
      negativeId: R1_Output
    - id: level15_green_branch_current
      title: Green Branch Current Safe
      description: 470 ohm fixed resistor must conduct approximately 5.5 to 7.0 mA
        with green LED forward-biased. Calibrate after measuring actual SparkLED
        model.
      kind: CurrentRange
      componentId: "Resistor_470_\u03A9"
      terminalId: 
      positiveId: Resistor_470_Input
      negativeId: Resistor_470_Output
    - id: level15_total_source_current
      title: Correct Total Source Current
      description: Total 5 V source current should be 14.0 to 17.0 mA once both branches
        conduct. Calibrate if the green LED forward voltage differs.
      kind: CurrentRange
      componentId: PowerSupply_01
      terminalId: 
      positiveId: Battery_positive
      negativeId: Battery_negative
  - levelNumber: 16
    chapterNumber: 1
    previousLevel: 15
    accessScore: 80
    inCampaign: 1
    chapterOpen: 1
    id: level_16
    title: Series LED Current Challenge
    description: Build a single series path from a switched 5 V source through replaceable
      100 ohm resistor, red LED and green LED, then back to ground. Replace the incorrect
      330 ohm resistor with 100 ohm in Register_Slot_2. Observe that both LEDs carry
      the same current and their forward voltage drops add. Verify both LEDs conduct,
      resistor current and voltage, and supply current. Power off before replacing
      parts. Nominal ranges assume approximately 2 V forward drop for each LED; calibrate
      with actual SparkLED model.
    conditions: Complete all configured objectives. A closed return path is required.
      Source shorts block completion. Target shorts block completion.
    sourceGuid: c6e74415442d6994ea9cdc11fd6168fb
    sourcePath: Assets/My_Assets/_Project_Spark/Prefabs/Levels/Chapter_02/Level_16_Layout/Level_16.asset
