      negativeId: R_LIMIT_Output
  - levelNumber: 27
    chapterNumber: 2
    previousLevel: 26
    accessScore: 80
    inCampaign: 1
    chapterOpen: 0
    id: level_27
    title: Charge the Reservoir - Capacitor Smoothing
    description: Build a 5 V DC diode-isolated reservoir circuit. A 220 ohm charging
      resistor feeds a 1000 uF capacitor and a 330 ohm LED load branch. Observe capacitor
      charging and confirm the stable output. This level demonstrates DC energy storage,
      not AC ripple suppression.
    conditions: Complete all configured objectives. A closed return path is required.
      Source shorts block completion. Target shorts block completion. Required installed
      resistors must be healthy.
    sourceGuid: 7475e73d8b0f97d48a83f4384f7b0dc5
    sourcePath: Assets/My_Assets/_Project_Spark/Prefabs/Levels/Chapter_03/Level_27_Layout/Level_27.asset
    chapter: Electronic Components
    accessRule: CompletePreviousChapter
    layoutPath: Assets/My_Assets/_Project_Spark/Prefabs/Levels/Chapter_03/Level_27_Layout/Level_27_Layout.prefab
    objectives:
    - "Stable 5 V Supply. Confirm the 5 V DC source. voltage \u2265 4.8 V. voltage
      \u2264 5.2 V. Connection pair Battery_positive and Battery_negative."
    - "Protection Diode Forward. Confirm the diode is forward biased. voltage \u2265
      0.45 V. voltage \u2264 1 V. Connection pair D_ISOLATE_Anode and D_ISOLATE_Cathode."
    - "Capacitor Charged. Confirm reservoir capacitor voltage reaches 3.1 to 3.7
      V in this loaded DC circuit. voltage \u2265 3.1 V. voltage \u2264 3.7 V. Connection
      pair C_RESERVOIR_Positive and C_RESERVOIR_Negative."
    - Indicator LED ON. Confirm the indicator LED glows when the capacitor rail supplies
      the load. Connection pair LED_Anode and LED_Cathode.
    - "Safe LED Branch Current. Verify approximately 3-6 mA through the 330 ohm LED
      resistor. current \u2265 3 mA. current \u2264 6 mA. Connection pair R_LED_Input
      and R_LED_Output."
    - "Charging Resistor Voltage. Check approximately 0.7-1.2 V drop across the 220
      ohm charging resistor after settling. voltage \u2265 0.7 V. voltage \u2264
      1.2 V. Connection pair R_CHARGE_Input and R_CHARGE_Output."
    equipment: []
    concepts:
    - Ohm law
    - Polarity
    - Rail qualification
    teachingResources: []
    targets:
