  - levelNumber: 28
    chapterNumber: 2
    previousLevel: 27
    accessScore: 80
    inCampaign: 1
    chapterOpen: 0
    id: level_28
    title: Emergency Power Backup - SPDT Capacitor Challenge
    description: 'Build a 5 V emergency backup circuit: 1N5819 Schottky diode, 220
      ohm charge resistor, 4700 uF storage capacitor, 330 ohm LED resistor, 1 kohm
      bleed resistor, and a three-terminal SPDT charge/backup selector. Charge in
      A-COM mode, switch source OFF, then select COM-B to power the LED from stored
      energy. Static targets sample BACKUP state only; phase sequence and discharge
      duration require a Level 28 local transient/phase driver.'
    conditions: Complete all configured objectives. Source shorts block completion.
      Target shorts block completion. Required installed resistors must be healthy.
    sourceGuid: 75390d3d0093ca24e9ddbb96f80641f5
    sourcePath: Assets/My_Assets/_Project_Spark/Prefabs/Levels/Chapter_03/Level_28_Layout/Level_28.asset
    chapter: Electronic Components
    accessRule: CompletePreviousChapter
    layoutPath: Assets/My_Assets/_Project_Spark/Prefabs/Levels/Chapter_03/Level_28_Layout/Level_28_Layout.prefab
    objectives:
    - "5 V Supply Available. Verify fixed 5 V supply. A voltage reading alone does
      not prove the source switch is OFF. voltage \u2265 4.8 V. voltage \u2264 5.2
      V. Connection pair Battery_positive and Battery_negative."
    - "Stored Backup Voltage. BACKUP snapshot: storage capacitor is energized. Requires
      level-local transient support to retain charge with main switch OFF. voltage
      \u2265 2.8 V. voltage \u2264 4.9 V. Connection pair C_BACKUP_Positive and C_BACKUP_Negative."
    - 'Backup LED Illuminated. BACKUP snapshot: green LED illuminates from the isolated
      stored energy. Connection pair LED_Anode and LED_Cathode.'
    - "Safe Backup LED Current. BACKUP snapshot: 2-12 mA flowing through the 330
      ohm LED limiting resistor. current \u2265 2 mA. current \u2264 12 mA. Connection
      pair R_LED_Input and R_LED_Output."
    - "1 kOhm Discharge Load Active. BACKUP snapshot: 2.8-4.9 mA in the 1 kohm bleed
      resistor at 2.8-4.9 V. current \u2265 2.8 mA. current \u2264 4.9 mA. Connection
      pair R_BLEED_Input and R_BLEED_Output."
    - "LED Resistor Voltage. BACKUP snapshot: voltage across the 330 ohm LED resistor
      indicates the LED branch is active. voltage \u2265 0.6 V. voltage \u2264 3.8
      V. Connection pair R_LED_Input and R_LED_Output."
    equipment: []
    concepts:
    - Closed path
    - Ohm law
    - Polarity
    teachingResources: []
    targets:
    - id: level28_supply
      title: 5 V Supply Available
      description: Verify fixed 5 V supply. A voltage reading alone does not prove
        the source switch is OFF.
      kind: VoltageRange
      componentId: PowerSupply_01
      terminalId: 
      positiveId: Battery_positive
      negativeId: Battery_negative
    - id: level28_cap_backup_voltage
      title: Stored Backup Voltage
      description: 'BACKUP snapshot: storage capacitor is energized. Requires level-local
        transient support to retain charge with main switch OFF.'
      kind: VoltageRange
      componentId: C_BACKUP_Component
      terminalId: 
      positiveId: C_BACKUP_Positive
      negativeId: C_BACKUP_Negative
    - id: level28_backup_led_on
      title: Backup LED Illuminated
      description: 'BACKUP snapshot: green LED illuminates from the isolated stored
        energy.'
      kind: LEDOn
      componentId: led
      terminalId: 
      positiveId: LED_Anode
      negativeId: LED_Cathode
    - id: level28_led_branch_current
      title: Safe Backup LED Current
      description: 'BACKUP snapshot: 2-12 mA flowing through the 330 ohm LED limiting
        resistor.'
      kind: CurrentRange
      componentId: R_LED_Component
      terminalId: 
      positiveId: R_LED_Input
      negativeId: R_LED_Output
    - id: level28_bleed_branch_current
      title: 1 kOhm Discharge Load Active
      description: 'BACKUP snapshot: 2.8-4.9 mA in the 1 kohm bleed resistor at 2.8-4.9
        V.'
      kind: CurrentRange
      componentId: R_BLEED_Component
      terminalId: 
      positiveId: R_BLEED_Input
      negativeId: R_BLEED_Output
    - id: level28_led_resistor_drop
      title: LED Resistor Voltage
      description: 'BACKUP snapshot: voltage across the 330 ohm LED resistor indicates
        the LED branch is active.'
      kind: VoltageRange
      componentId: R_LED_Component
      terminalId: 
      positiveId: R_LED_Input
      negativeId: R_LED_Output
  - levelNumber: 29
    chapterNumber: 2
    previousLevel: 28
    accessScore: 80
    inCampaign: 1
    chapterOpen: 0
    id: level_29
    title: Automatic Emergency Backup - No Manual Transfer
    description: Build a three-diode automatic capacitor backup. Verify charging,
      isolate the mains with the main switch, sustain LED backup for 2 accepted simulated
      seconds, then restore power and recharge. SparkLevel29AutomaticBackup validates
      the sequence and publishes six runtime LED gate aliases. No SPDT is used. Without
      the observer the level cannot complete.
    conditions: Complete all configured objectives. A closed return path is required.
      Source shorts block completion. Target shorts block completion. Required installed
      resistors must be healthy.
    sourceGuid: 2e4bc1d5117b4e744ab6e32d6970c3a9
    sourcePath: Assets/My_Assets/_Project_Spark/Prefabs/Levels/Chapter_03/Level_29_Layout/Level_29.asset
    chapter: Electronic Components
    accessRule: CompletePreviousChapter
    layoutPath: Assets/My_Assets/_Project_Spark/Prefabs/Levels/Chapter_03/Level_29_Layout/Level_29_Layout.prefab
    objectives:
    - "Correct automatic-backup circuit. Required nets, values and healthy parts
      verified by the level observer. current \u2265 2 mA. Conduction required."
    - "Storage charged with observed rise. Capacitor rises at least 0.30 V and reaches
      4.10 V. current \u2265 2 mA. Conduction required."
    - "Automatic isolated transfer. MAIN is open; backup diode powers LED while main/charge/source
      current stays below 0.10 mA. current \u2265 2 mA. Conduction required."
    - "Sustained backup power. LED current at least 2 mA for 2 accepted simulated
      seconds, capacitor drops at least 0.20 V. current \u2265 2 mA. Conduction required."
    - "Main power restored and charging. MAIN restored, load powered by main diode
      and positive charging current observed. current \u2265 2 mA. Conduction required."
    - "Recovered normal operation. Capacitor rises at least 0.15 V after restoration,
      reaches 4.10 V and remains normal for 0.5 simulated seconds. current \u2265
      2 mA. Conduction required."
    equipment: []
    concepts:
    - Closed path
    - Ohm law
    - Polarity
    teachingResources: []
    targets:
    - id: level29_auto_0
      title: Correct automatic-backup circuit
      description: Required nets, values and healthy parts verified by the level
        observer.
      kind: LEDOn
      componentId: L29_Wiring
      terminalId: 
      positiveId: 
      negativeId: 
    - id: level29_auto_1
      title: Storage charged with observed rise
      description: Capacitor rises at least 0.30 V and reaches 4.10 V.
      kind: LEDOn
      componentId: L29_Charged
      terminalId: 
      positiveId: 
      negativeId: 
    - id: level29_auto_2
      title: Automatic isolated transfer
      description: MAIN is open; backup diode powers LED while main/charge/source
        current stays below 0.10 mA.
      kind: LEDOn
      componentId: L29_Isolated
      terminalId: 
      positiveId: 
      negativeId: 
    - id: level29_auto_3
      title: Sustained backup power
      description: LED current at least 2 mA for 2 accepted simulated seconds, capacitor
        drops at least 0.20 V.
      kind: LEDOn
      componentId: L29_Backup
      terminalId: 
      positiveId: 
      negativeId: 
    - id: level29_auto_4
      title: Main power restored and charging
      description: MAIN restored, load powered by main diode and positive charging
        current observed.
      kind: LEDOn
      componentId: L29_Restored
      terminalId: 
      positiveId: 
      negativeId: 
    - id: level29_auto_5
      title: Recovered normal operation
      description: Capacitor rises at least 0.15 V after restoration, reaches 4.10
        V and remains normal for 0.5 simulated seconds.
      kind: LEDOn
      componentId: L29_Recharged
      terminalId: 
      positiveId: 
      negativeId: 
