  - levelNumber: 94
    chapterNumber: 10
    previousLevel: 93
    accessScore: 80
    inCampaign: 1
    chapterOpen: 0
    id: level_94
    title: The Board Foundry
    description: Build and qualify a two-layer PCB, repair three faults, and recover
      the removable W035 jumper.
    conditions: Complete all configured objectives. Source shorts block completion.
      Target shorts block completion.
    sourceGuid: 3c9438fd0c0990f4a99307ba29824965
    sourcePath: Assets/My_Assets/_Project_Spark/Prefabs/Levels/Level_94_Layout/Level_94.asset
    chapter: PCB Engineering
    accessRule: CompletePreviousChapter
    layoutPath: Assets/My_Assets/_Project_Spark/Prefabs/Levels/Level_94_Layout/Level_94_Layout.prefab
    objectives:
    - Inspect the PCB schematic and nets. Review the 34 route entries in the board
      netlist before fitting the first part.
    - Install all 27 components. Choose each matching component, align its pin-1
      mark, fit it, and solder the footprint contacts.
    - Route 34 copper tasks and plate six vias. Connect W001 through W034 between
      the indicated native pads and plate V01 through V06 on the two-layer board.
    - Commission the protected board. Fit W035, enable the protected virtual bench,
      record live 3.3 V and feedback, and qualify a fresh load-current sample.
    - Repair all three faults and retest. Diagnose the open V05, incorrect R2 value
      and Q1 bridge. Isolate power for each repair and verify a fresh run.
    - Recover W035 feedback and requalify. Interrupt W035 with power on, confirm
      that the load is inhibited, restore feedback, reset the latch, and qualify
      again.
    equipment: []
    concepts: []
    teachingResources: []
    targets:
    - id: level94_pcb_1
      title: Inspect the PCB schematic and nets
      description: Review the 34 route entries in the board netlist before fitting
        the first part.
