  - levelNumber: 95
    chapterNumber: 10
    previousLevel: 94
    accessScore: 80
    inCampaign: 1
    chapterOpen: 0
    id: level_95
    title: The Pulse Architect
    description: Build a precision timing controller, measure its clocks and PWM,
      and recover the W049 safety feedback.
    conditions: Complete all configured objectives. Source shorts block completion.
      Target shorts block completion.
    sourceGuid: a3ecafe8c24521a4c8ef07ef476452be
    sourcePath: Assets/My_Assets/_Project_Spark/Prefabs/Levels/Level_95_Layout/Level_95.asset
    chapter: PCB Engineering
    accessRule: CompletePreviousChapter
    layoutPath: Assets/My_Assets/_Project_Spark/Prefabs/Levels/Level_95_Layout/Level_95_Layout.prefab
    objectives:
    - Inspect and assemble the timing board. Review the timing netlist, then select,
      align and solder all 35 fixed components.
    - Route 48 traces, plate 10 vias and fit W049. Route the 48 specified traces
      through the original pads and ten vias. Install W049 as the separate 36th part.
    - Capture and qualify the three clocks. Capture the powered master and divided
      clocks near 1024 Hz, 256 Hz and 2 Hz.
    - Verify 25%, 50% and 75% PWM under load. Capture 25%, 50% and 75% PWM and verify
      both solved load states for each setting.
    - Repair all three timing faults and retest. Diagnose and isolate V06, C1 and
      the Q1 bridge in sequence. Capture a fresh powered result after each repair.
    - Recover W049 feedback and requalify. Remove W049 while powered, prove output
      inhibit, restore feedback, acknowledge the latch and capture again.
    equipment: []
    concepts:
    - Measurement
    - Timing and interlocks
    teachingResources:
    - d6183c80385c7aa46933364d09bb4b64
