    id: level_128
    title: The AORUS Master
    description: Service the AM5 training board, prove GPU and NVMe lane sharing,
      isolate three faults and qualify a protected return to service.
    conditions: Complete all configured objectives. Source shorts block completion.
      Target shorts block completion.
    sourceGuid: 28b80c5216033d44d9014da7b58a88eb
    sourcePath: Assets/My_Assets/_Project_Spark/Prefabs/Levels/Level_128_Layout/Level_128.asset
    chapter: Commercial Motherboards
    accessRule: CompletePreviousChapter
    layoutPath: Assets/My_Assets/_Project_Spark/Prefabs/Levels/Level_128_Layout/Level_128_Layout.prefab
    objectives:
    - Assemble the isolated AM5 system. Key the AM5 CPU, cross-mount its cooler,
      latch A2/B2 and secure the M.2 A boot drive.
    - Sequence dual EPS and power-good. Verify standby, both EPS inputs, power-good
      and every loaded regulated test point.
    - Train A2/B2 and complete a fresh POST. Verify CPU, both memory channels, graphics
      and boot storage in order.
    - "Qualify the GPU lane bank and four M.2 sockets. Prove GPU \xD716 with A alone,
      \xD716 with A+D and \xD78 with all drives. Verify every M.2 link."
    - Identify and verify three physical repairs. Use measurements to find VRM_Q03,
      DDR5_A2 and M2B_CPU. Isolate and inspect before fitting each spare.
    - Prove protection and two isolated restarts. Prove shutdown during loaded fan
      loss. Restore cooling, reset, verify two cold boots and qualify thermal recovery.
    equipment: []
    concepts:
    - Closed path
    teachingResources: []
