    summary: POWER SSUPPLY POSETIVE TO LED ANODE. AND POWER SUPPLY NEGATIVE TO LED
      CATHHODE. LIGHT SHOULD BE ON
  - kind: SparkLevelDefinition
    name: LIGHT THE BULB
    guid: a3bff753f4100dc44a5bf10b3b9fa418
    path: Assets/My_Assets/_Project_Spark/Prefabs/Levels/Chapter_01/Level_02_Layout/Level_02.asset
    summary: POWER SSUPPLY POSETIVE TO LED ANODE. AND POWER SUPPLY NEGATIVE TO LED
      CATHHODE. LIGHT SHOULD BE ON
  - kind: SparkLevelDefinition
    name: The Current Limiter
    guid: e6a958e6cd2dd3347a75295b9f4325e3
    path: Assets/My_Assets/_Project_Spark/Prefabs/Levels/Chapter_01/Level_03_Layout/Level_03.asset
    summary: Build a circuit with a current-limiting resistor LIGHT SHOULD BE ON
  - kind: SparkLevelDefinition
    name: The Power Challenge
    guid: 5a0d4a75714c7d64dae8c0ace7b19e52
    path: Assets/My_Assets/_Project_Spark/Prefabs/Levels/Chapter_01/Level_04_Layout/Level_04.asset
    summary: Light the LED while controlling current and resistor power.
  - kind: SparkLevelDefinition
    name: Parallel Paths
    guid: de819af5483f27d47a49466238e08428
    path: Assets/My_Assets/_Project_Spark/Prefabs/Levels/Chapter_01/Level_05_Layout/Level_05.asset
    summary: Power two LEDs in parallel while controlling branch and total current.
  - kind: SparkLevelDefinition
    name: Circuit Fault Detective
    guid: 49d903f6d8ca9a44abfbd0e34dde1942
    path: Assets/My_Assets/_Project_Spark/Prefabs/Levels/Chapter_01/Level_06_Layout/Level_06.asset
    summary: A parallel LED circuit has two faults. One branch has a missing connection,
      and the other contains an unsuitable resistor. Inspect the circuit, repair
      the connection, select the correct resistor, and bring both LEDs into their
      safe operating ranges.
  - kind: SparkLevelDefinition
    name: Voltage Divider Challenge
    guid: 7f8591594dc74ab45a14ecd6fdf4cc5d
    path: Assets/My_Assets/_Project_Spark/Prefabs/Levels/Chapter_01/Level_07_Layout/Level_07.asset
    summary: Calibrate a 3.00 V output from a 5 V supply by selecting the correct
      upper resistor.
  - kind: SparkLevelDefinition
    name: Voltage Divider Challenge
    guid: 53f2e48aabcb06d409bbdf086c3dad9d
    path: Assets/My_Assets/_Project_Spark/Prefabs/Levels/Chapter_01/Level_08_Layout/Level_08.asset
    summary: Calibrate a 3.00 V output from a 5 V supply by selecting the correct
      upper resistor.
  - kind: SparkLevelDefinition
    name: "Series\u2013Parallel Circuit Master"
    guid: c079580d6a66e3b43ab755f0798075dd
    path: Assets/My_Assets/_Project_Spark/Prefabs/Levels/Chapter_01/Level_09_Layout/Level_09.asset
    summary: "Build a 5 V series-parallel circuit: R1 = 220 \u03A9 in series with
      parallel R2 = 330 \u03A9 and R3 = 470 \u03A9. Achieve approximately 2.342 V
      at VOUT and 12.081 mA total current."
  - kind: SparkLevelDefinition
    name: Bridge Balance Challenge
    guid: 794004c63cb1b9643b5389bd22d9a311
    path: Assets/My_Assets/_Project_Spark/Prefabs/Levels/Chapter_01/Level_10_Layout/Level_10.asset
    summary: "Balance two voltage dividers on a 5 V supply. Replace the upper-right
      resistor with 100 \u03A9 until the LCD measures approximately 0.00 V between
      their midpoint nodes."
  - kind: SparkLevelDefinition
    name: Power Distribution Challenge
    guid: 75dca85951b518543a34f15d67e5654f
    path: Assets/My_Assets/_Project_Spark/Prefabs/Levels/Chapter_02/Level_11_Layout/Level_11.asset
    summary: Restore a safe 5 V three-branch parallel power network. Replace the
      overloaded 100 ohm R2 with 220 ohm; verify approximately 22.73 mA through R2,
      5.00 V across R2, and 48.52 mA total source current. Turn the switch off before
      replacing resistors.
  - kind: SparkLevelDefinition
    name: "Series\u2013Parallel Circuit Challenge"
    guid: 61ceade98407dd34ea1c184441b1cb7d
    path: Assets/My_Assets/_Project_Spark/Prefabs/Levels/Chapter_02/Level_12_Layout/Level_12.asset
    summary: 'Build a 5 V series-parallel network: fixed 330 ohm R1 in one branch,
      and replaceable R2 in series with fixed 470 ohm R3 in the other. Replace incorrect
      100 ohm R2 with 220 ohm, measure 3.41 V across R3, verify 7.25 mA in the series
      branch and approximately 22.40 mA total source current. Switch off before replacing
      a resistor.'
  - kind: SparkLevelDefinition
    name: Loaded Voltage Divider Challenge
    guid: dbdd5c7e9d81df049b1f7abde04561fe
    path: Assets/My_Assets/_Project_Spark/Prefabs/Levels/Chapter_02/Level_13_Layout/Level_13.asset
    summary: 'Build a loaded 5 V voltage divider: a fixed 220 ohm R1 in series with
      a parallel load formed by replaceable R2 and fixed 470 ohm R3. Replace the
      incorrect 150 ohm R2 with 330 ohm. Measure 2.34 V at Vout, verify approximately
      7.10 mA in R2 and 12.08 mA total source current. Switch power off before replacing
      components.'
  - kind: SparkLevelDefinition
    name: LED Protection & Current Limiting
    guid: da2d255690cf0ac4c94790d498db8033
    path: Assets/My_Assets/_Project_Spark/Prefabs/Levels/Chapter_02/Level_14_Layout/Level_14.asset
    summary: Build a 5 V parallel circuit. Branch A has a replaceable resistor in
      series with a correctly oriented red LED; branch B has a fixed 470 ohm resistor.
      Replace the incorrect 150 ohm resistor with 330 ohm to limit LED-branch current
      to about 9.09 mA (assuming LED forward voltage 2.0 V). Verify about 3.0 V across
      the resistor and 19.73 mA total source current. Switch power off before replacing
      components.
  - kind: SparkLevelDefinition
    name: Dual LED Parallel Circuit Challenge
    guid: 6284c7018244ffb4a842917d2c9049f8
    path: Assets/My_Assets/_Project_Spark/Prefabs/Levels/Chapter_02/Level_15_Layout/Level_15.asset
    summary: 'Build two independent LED branches in parallel from a switched 5 V
      supply. Branch A uses a replaceable resistor: replace the incorrect 150 ohm
      with 330 ohm in Register_Slot_2, then connect the red LED in series. Branch
      B uses a fixed 470 ohm resistor in series with a green LED; correct its polarity.
      Both LED cathodes return to supply negative. Verify both LEDs conduct, each
      branch current is within its target range, and total source current is correct.
      Switch power off before changing parts. Green LED targets depend on its configured
      forward-voltage model.'
  - kind: SparkLevelDefinition
    name: Series LED Current Challenge
    guid: c6e74415442d6994ea9cdc11fd6168fb
    path: Assets/My_Assets/_Project_Spark/Prefabs/Levels/Chapter_02/Level_16_Layout/Level_16.asset
    summary: Build a single series path from a switched 5 V source through replaceable
      100 ohm resistor, red LED and green LED, then back to ground. Replace the incorrect
      330 ohm resistor with 100 ohm in Register_Slot_2. Observe that both LEDs carry
      the same current and their forward voltage drops add. Verify both LEDs conduct,
      resistor current and voltage, and supply current. Power off before replacing
      parts. Nominal ranges assume approximately 2 V forward drop for each LED; calibrate
      with actual SparkLED model.
  - kind: SparkLevelDefinition
    name: "Series\u2013Parallel LED Network"
    guid: 56317e55910cbab478e1fe12eb7b6314
    path: Assets/My_Assets/_Project_Spark/Prefabs/Levels/Chapter_02/Level_17_Layout/Level_17.asset
    summary: 'From a switched 5 V supply, install a 100 ohm series resistor in Register_Slot_2.
      After this resistor split into two parallel branches: 330 ohm + red LED, and
      470 ohm + green LED. Reconnect both LED cathodes to supply negative. Check
      both LEDs, each branch current, and source current. Power off before replacing
      the initial 220 ohm resistor. Current thresholds are nominal and must be checked
      against the actual SparkLED solver.'
  - kind: SparkLevelDefinition
    name: Precision Voltage Divider
    guid: a67073b969181e143bc30359baadb0e3
    path: Assets/My_Assets/_Project_Spark/Prefabs/Levels/Chapter_02/Level_18_Layout/Level_18.asset
    summary: From a 5 V switched DC source, build a series voltage divider with a
      330 ohm TOP resistor and a 470 ohm BOTTOM resistor. Connect supply positive
      through the switch and TOP resistor to VOUT, then through the BOTTOM resistor
      to supply negative. Measure VOUT relative to negative (~2.94 V), confirm the
      voltage across each resistor, and confirm equal series currents (~6.25 mA).
      Power off before changing components. Nominal thresholds should be verified
      with the Project Spark solver.
  - kind: SparkLevelDefinition
    name: The Loading Effect
    guid: da56e283820aca043a09387e293bbabb
    path: Assets/My_Assets/_Project_Spark/Prefabs/Levels/Chapter_02/Level_19_Layout/Level_19.asset
    summary: 'From a switched 5 V DC supply, build a 330 ohm TOP resistor in series
      with a parallel pair: a 470 ohm BOTTOM resistor and a 1 kohm LOAD resistor.
      Connect supply positive through the switch and TOP resistor to VOUT. Connect
      both BOTTOM and LOAD inputs to VOUT and both outputs to supply negative. Measure
      VOUT relative to negative (nominal ~2.46 V), and verify TOP, BOTTOM, LOAD and
      source currents (~7.70, ~5.24, ~2.46 and ~7.70 mA). Switch power off before
      changing connections. Verify ranges against the Project Spark solver.'
  - kind: SparkLevelDefinition
    name: Wheatstone Bridge Balance
    guid: 3e519535634e7db4fbda3ed1044e16f6
    path: Assets/My_Assets/_Project_Spark/Prefabs/Levels/Chapter_02/Level_20_Layout/Level_20.asset
    summary: 'From a switched 5 V supply, build two parallel voltage dividers: LEFT
      330 ohm TOP and 470 ohm BOTTOM, RIGHT 330 ohm TOP and 470 ohm BOTTOM. The RIGHT
      TOP workstation initially has an incorrect 220 ohm resistor; power off, replace
      it with 330 ohm, and wire both branches to the common supply positive and negative.
      Measure the difference between MID A (left midpoint) and MID B (right midpoint)
      using LCD Terminals A and B, not a conducting wire. Balance requires near-zero
      midpoint difference, both midpoint voltages near 2.94 V, two branch currents
      near 6.25 mA, and total source current near 12.5 mA. Verify values against
      the Project Spark solver.'
  - kind: SparkLevelDefinition
    name: Capacitor Charge - Store the Energy
    guid: c708ffba3a0f40b498e534c36a0b1e16
    path: Assets/My_Assets/_Project_Spark/Prefabs/Levels/Chapter_03/Level_21_Layout/Level_21.asset
    summary: Build a 5 V RC charging circuit with a 1 kOhm resistor and 1000 uF capacitor.
      Charge the capacitor near 5 V and verify that the charging resistor voltage
      drop settles near zero.
  - kind: SparkLevelDefinition
    name: One Way Only - Diode Direction
    guid: f8bef5aa235d0c54c862ca4d4861addb
    path: Assets/My_Assets/_Project_Spark/Prefabs/Levels/Chapter_03/Level_22_Layout/Level_22.asset
    summary: Build a 5 V forward-biased diode and green LED indicator circuit. Identify
      anode and cathode, place the 1N4007 correctly, and confirm safe LED current.
  - kind: SparkLevelDefinition
    name: Triple Barrier - Three Diodes in Series
    guid: 5f8a61257c5fa644da55090427b0ecfb
    path: Assets/My_Assets/_Project_Spark/Prefabs/Levels/Chapter_03/Level_23_Layout/Level_23.asset
    summary: Build a 5 V circuit using a 150 ohm current-limiting resistor, three
      forward-biased 1N4007 diodes in series, and a green LED. Verify diode polarity,
      safe current, and illumination.
  - kind: SparkLevelDefinition
    name: Opposite Directions - Diode Challenge
    guid: 269fbcb35223f9248865f22ee4775375
    path: Assets/My_Assets/_Project_Spark/Prefabs/Levels/Chapter_03/Level_24_Layout/Level_24.asset
    summary: Build a 5 V circuit using a 330 ohm resistor and two antiparallel 1N4007
      diodes. The forward diode must conduct, the reverse diode must block, and the
      green LED must illuminate at safe current.
  - kind: SparkLevelDefinition
    name: Dual Path Power - Diode OR Gate
    guid: 76ab9d51a4e62a74ca59edfdddf98f50
    path: Assets/My_Assets/_Project_Spark/Prefabs/Levels/Chapter_03/Level_25_Layout/Level_25.asset
    summary: Build a 5 V diode OR gate using two independently controlled switches,
      two forward-biased 1N4007 diodes, a common 330 ohm resistor, and a green LED.
      With switch A ON and switch B OFF, verify the forward path and safe current.
      Test the other switch states using the truth table.
  - kind: SparkLevelDefinition
    name: Bridge Defender - Four Diode Rectifier
    guid: 4b48503581b02294c8ef750ebf53c660
    path: Assets/My_Assets/_Project_Spark/Prefabs/Levels/Chapter_03/Level_26_Layout/Level_26.asset
    summary: Build a 5 V DC four-diode bridge rectifier. Forward diodes D1 and D4
      deliver current through a 220 ohm resistor and green LED while D2 and D3 block.
      Verify bridge polarity, safe series current and the illuminated LED.
  - kind: SparkLevelDefinition
    name: Charge the Reservoir - Capacitor Smoothing
    guid: 7475e73d8b0f97d48a83f4384f7b0dc5
    path: Assets/My_Assets/_Project_Spark/Prefabs/Levels/Chapter_03/Level_27_Layout/Level_27.asset
    summary: Build a 5 V DC diode-isolated reservoir circuit. A 220 ohm charging
      resistor feeds a 1000 uF capacitor and a 330 ohm LED load branch. Observe capacitor
      charging and confirm the stable output. This level demonstrates DC energy storage,
      not AC ripple suppression.
  - kind: SparkLevelDefinition
    name: Emergency Power Backup - SPDT Capacitor Challenge
    guid: 75390d3d0093ca24e9ddbb96f80641f5
    path: Assets/My_Assets/_Project_Spark/Prefabs/Levels/Chapter_03/Level_28_Layout/Level_28.asset
    summary: 'Build a 5 V emergency backup circuit: 1N5819 Schottky diode, 220 ohm
      charge resistor, 4700 uF storage capacitor, 330 ohm LED resistor, 1 kohm bleed
      resistor, and a three-terminal SPDT charge/backup selector. Charge in A-COM
      mode, switch source OFF, then select COM-B to power the LED from stored energy.
      Static targets sample BACKUP state only; phase sequence and discharge duration
      require a Level 28 local transient/phase driver.'
  - kind: SparkLevelDefinition
    name: Automatic Emergency Backup - No Manual Transfer
    guid: 2e4bc1d5117b4e744ab6e32d6970c3a9
    path: Assets/My_Assets/_Project_Spark/Prefabs/Levels/Chapter_03/Level_29_Layout/Level_29.asset
    summary: Build a three-diode automatic capacitor backup. Verify charging, isolate
      the mains with the main switch, sustain LED backup for 2 accepted simulated
      seconds, then restore power and recharge. SparkLevel29AutomaticBackup validates
      the sequence and publishes six runtime LED gate aliases. No SPDT is used. Without
      the observer the level cannot complete.
  - kind: SparkLevelDefinition
    name: Elevate the Lamp - Motor Control and Limit Switches
    guid: 09947b5992b753a4791e1e6d3c25490d
    path: Assets/My_Assets/_Project_Spark/Prefabs/Levels/Chapter_03/Level_30_Layout/Level_30.asset
    summary: Wire a reversible lift. Verify both end stops, the top-only lamp, and
      a complete UP/DOWN round trip.
